  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A staff cut from a tree older than any forest now standing. It puts out a single green leaf each spring, in whatever country it happens to be, and drops it again in the fall.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon.</p><p>You can use this staff as a Spellcasting Focus. While you hold it you can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPlantGrowt]{Plant Growth} at will.</p><p><strong>Wake the Wood.</strong> Once per day, as an action, you strike the staff against a tree of Huge size or smaller within 60 feet. The tree wakes as a Treant under the GM's control, friendly to you, and fights beside you for 1 hour before it roots itself again. The staff regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>The Wood Speaks.</strong> Whoever holds the staff can speak with any tree and be answered. Trees remember centuries and little else: who passed, what was buried, when the fire came. They are slow to start and slower to stop.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
